            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0386" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2255a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-20T17:00:00-05:00">October 20, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>109. 1. Referring to our telephone conversation of this morning, I authorize you
                    to continue sitting in the open meetings of the Council and in the seat at the
                    table which has been assigned you. It is my understanding that you will attend
                    no more secret meetings and that at the public meetings your role will be
                    strictly that of an observer.</p>
                <p>2. I shall study the text of the telegram which you read me in lieu of cabling,
                    when the stenographic record becomes available to me.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
